<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Oct 17 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>Unknown     331,600			   Nil</p>
<p>China	 287,800</p>
<p>Netherlands 207,100-A</p>
<p>Taiwan	145,100</p>
<p>A-includes 50,000 in destination changes.</p>
<p>Net sales of 1,394,500 tonnes were 20 percent above last week's marketing year high, 81 percent above the four-week average and only six percent less than the all-time weekly record of 1,484,300 tonnes for the week ending Nov. 12, 1987.</p>
<p>Exports of 595,700 tonnes -- a marketing year high -- were more than three times the previous week and more than double the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Germany (109,400), Japan (95,600), Spain (92,000), Mexico (83,500) and the Netherlands (64,400).</p>
</text>
